title: '[pallet-revive] Derive child trie ids from the deletion queue counter'

doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The child trie id of a new contract is now derived from its address, the deployer's nonce and
    the insert counter of the deletion queue, instead of the address and the deployer's nonce
    only. A contract created at the address of a terminated contract therefore never shares the
    terminated contract's storage, also while that storage is still waiting in the deletion queue.

    Existing contracts keep their trie ids, and queued deletions are unchanged.

    Off-chain tools that compute a contract's trie id from its address and the deployer's nonce
    must read `trie_id` from the contract's `ContractInfo` in `AccountInfoOf` instead. The id of a
    new contract cannot be computed without the deletion queue counter at the time it was
    created.

- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    No migration or configuration change is needed. The storage layout is unchanged.

    Creating a contract now also reads `DeletionQueueCounter`. This affects the weights of
    `instantiate`, `instantiate_with_code`, `eth_instantiate_with_code`, `seal_instantiate` and
    `evm_instantiate`. Runtimes should regenerate their `pallet_revive` weights.

    The `RedeployFactory` fixture is new and adds the `RedeployFactory`, `RedeployChild` and
    `RedeployDeployer` modules to `pallet-revive-fixtures`.

crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
